{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"ATTESTATION RECIPE — why the criterion is still open and exactly how to close it.\n\nThe AC wants a full rebar review-plan run emitting ZERO cache warnings when caching is working,\nevidenced by the run's aggregate cache_write_tokens > 0.\n\nA live plan-review WAS run this session (on 0d76, after the fix landed on origin/main) and its coverage\nmetrics recorded cache_write_tokens 39473 and cache_read_tokens 225616 — both well above zero, so\ncaching was demonstrably working. That is most of the evidence. It is NOT cited as satisfying the\ncriterion because the run was not captured in a form that also proves the ZERO-WARNINGS half: the\nwarning is emitted to the log stream, and that run's output was not retained for warning inspection.\n\nRECIPE (a single run satisfies this AND 77ed's Pass-1 attestation):\n  export REBAR_USAGE_LOG=/tmp/rebar_usage.jsonl\n  rebar review-plan <any unblocked ticket> 2>&1 | tee /tmp/review_run.log\nthen cite, on this ticket: the aggregate cache_write_tokens from the verdict's coverage.metrics, the\nabsence of any warn_if_cache_ineffective line in /tmp/review_run.log, and a timestamp. Note the usage\nlog is OPT-IN — usage_log.py:29 ENV_VAR = 'REBAR_USAGE_LOG' — so without the export there is no\nper-step attribution to cite.\n\nReminder from the fix itself: the 4096-token floor is model-dependent and documented as the OPUS\nfloor, so a run below it legitimately emits no warning and would not prove the criterion either way —\nthe cited run must be above the floor, as the 0d76 run's 39473 cache_write_tokens comfortably was."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785699798039129001,"uuid":"acce1d62-ced8-4947-910c-af936a7d7fd8"}